  {
   "id": "de_a1_grammar",
   "type": "grammar",
   "title": "Articles, pronouns and the present tense",
   "lessons": [
    {
     "id": "de_a1_grammar_1",
     "title": "Articles, pronouns and the present tense",
     "summary": "der/die/das, ein/eine, personal pronouns, and regular verbs plus sein in the present tense.",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Every noun has a gender. The definite article (the) is der, die or das; the indefinite article (a) is ein (masculine/neuter) or eine (feminine)."
      },
      {
       "type": "table",
       "head": [
        "Gender",
        "the",
        "a"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "masculine",
         "der Tisch",
         "ein Tisch"
        ],
        [
         "feminine",
         "die Küche",
         "eine Küche"
        ],
        [
         "neuter",
         "das Bett",
         "ein Bett"
        ],
        [
         "plural",
         "die Tische",
         "– (no article)"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Regular verbs drop -en and add an ending for each person. sein (to be) is irregular and must be memorised."
      },
      {
       "type": "table",
       "head": [
        "Pronoun",
        "wohnen (to live)",
        "kommen (to come)",
        "sein (to be)"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "ich (I)",
         "wohne",
         "komme",
         "bin"
        ],
        [
         "du (you, informal)",
         "wohnst",
         "kommst",
         "bist"
        ],
        [
         "er / sie / es",
         "wohnt",
         "kommt",
         "ist"
        ],
        [
         "wir (we)",
         "wohnen",
         "kommen",
         "sind"
        ],
        [
         "ihr (you all)",
         "wohnt",
         "kommt",
         "seid"
        ],
        [
         "sie / Sie (they / you formal)",
         "wohnen",
         "kommen",
         "sind"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "tip",
       "text": "In a statement the verb is always the second element: Ich wohne in Berlin. / In Berlin wohne ich."
      },
      {
       "type": "example",
       "target": "Woher kommst du?",
       "en": "Where are you from?"
      },
      {
       "type": "example",
       "target": "Ich komme aus Indien.",
       "en": "I come from India."
      }
     ],
     "questions": [
      {
       "type": "fill",
       "prompt": "Ich ___ in Berlin. (wohnen)",
       "answers": [
        "wohne"
       ],
       "explanation": "ich → -e: ich wohne.",
       "id": "de_a1_grammar_1_q1",
       "skill": "grammar"
      },
      {
       "type": "fill",
       "prompt": "Du ___ sehr nett. (sein)",
       "answers": [
        "bist"
       ],
       "explanation": "du bist = you are.",
       "id": "de_a1_grammar_1_q2",
       "skill": "grammar"
      },
      {
       "type": "mcq",
       "prompt": "Wir ___ aus Spanien.",
       "options": [
        "kommt",
        "kommen",
        "komme"
       ],
       "answer": 1,
       "explanation": "wir → -en: wir kommen.",
       "id": "de_a1_grammar_1_q3",
       "skill": "grammar"
      },
      {
       "type": "correction",
       "prompt": "Er kommen aus Indien.",
       "answers": [
        "Er kommt aus Indien."
       ],
       "explanation": "er/sie/es takes -t: er kommt.",
       "skill": "grammar",
       "id": "de_a1_grammar_1_q4"
      },
      {
       "type": "order",
       "prompt": "",
       "words": [
        "Woher",
        "kommst",
        "du?"
       ],
       "explanation": "Question words come first, then the verb.",
       "translation": "Where are you from?",
       "id": "de_a1_grammar_1_q5",
       "skill": "grammar"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "de_a1_reading",
   "type": "reading",
   "title": "Reading: Lena introduces herself",
   "lessons": [
    {
     "id": "de_a1_reading_1",
     "title": "Reading: Lena introduces herself",
     "summary": "A short personal profile. Read it, then answer the questions.",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "passage",
       "title": "Lena stellt sich vor",
       "target": "Hallo! Ich heiße Lena und ich bin 25 Jahre alt. Ich komme aus Hamburg, aber ich wohne jetzt in München. Ich bin Lehrerin. Meine Wohnung ist klein, aber schön. Am Wochenende spiele ich gern Tennis.",
       "en": "Hello! My name is Lena and I am 25 years old. I come from Hamburg, but I live in Munich now. I am a teacher. My flat is small but nice. At the weekend I like playing tennis."
      },
      {
       "type": "tip",
       "text": "„gern“ after a verb means you like doing it: Ich spiele gern Tennis = I like playing tennis."
      }
     ],
     "questions": [
